      "text": "The diagonal \\( d \\) of a rectangular prism with side lengths \\( a \\), \\( b \\), and \\( c \\) is given by the formula:\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2 + c^2} \\]\nHere, the side lengths of the rectangular prism are \\( a = 10 \\) inches, \\( b = 20 \\) inches, and \\( c = 10 \\) inches. Substituting these values into the formula, we get:\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{10^2 + 20^2 + 10^2} \\]\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{100 + 400 + 100} \\]\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{600} \\]\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{100 \\times 6} \\]\n\\[ d = 10\\sqrt{6} \\]\nTherefore, the length of the diagonal connecting point \\( A \\) and point \\( B \\) is \\(\\boxed{10\\sqrt{6}}\\) inches.",
